Now that you have the full EPP picture, the goal is clear: **copy its structure (sections, tables, charts with legend tables) and swap the log data for our EGG metrics.**

## 1. How each EPP section maps to EGG

| EPP section | What it shows | EGG equivalent |
|---|---|---|
| **Workflow Lifecycle** (purple) | Global table (init, success, incomplete, success %, incomplete %), tenant table, charts: Initialize / Success / Incomplete / Success vs Errors | Same, **per workflow**. Tables group **by `env`** instead of tenant, because `workflow_init` has no `tenant_id`. Incomplete = init − success − failure. Charts: Started / Completed / Failed per workflow. |
| **Auth** (green) | Tenant table plus one chart per action | Replace with **Capture**, **Reversal**, **Tokenize & RemoveToken** and **Inquire** sections, each with a tenant table plus one chart per outcome metric |
| **Issues** (orange) | Error by Type, Payment Failures by Type, Issues by Tenant (error/critical/warning), Warning/Critical charts, Error trend | `issue` metrics by `error_code` (payment, reversal) and `error_context` (inquire), by `level`, by tenant. Warning and Critical charts get a "(pending RD-11640)" label. |
| **Payments** (blue) | Tenant table (init, success, decline, error, %), "payment_success" total tile, Init/Success/Decline/Error charts by entity | Exactly the same using `egg_payment.payment_*`, plus Auto reversal. Charts by `tenant_id`. |
| **Service Calls** (yellow) | Epic Interconnect GetSessionData and TransactionResult | **No EGG metric exists for this.** Turn it into **Processor Calls**: capture and reversal by `processor` (fusebox, freedompay). |
| Filters: env, log.tenant_id, log.root_entity_id, log.context.tenant_id | | Our 8: env, workflow_name, application, tenant_id, location_id, processor, reason, type |

